    "about": "A sample, not a machine record: copy this file to .agents/machine.local.json — the name .gitignore holds — and replace every __TOKEN__ with this machine's own value. The tokens are the facts a machine measures rather than the repository owning: the interpreter and its directory (__PHP_EXE__, __PHP_DIR__) with its version and whether a bare `php` resolves (__PHP_VERSION__, __PHP_ON_PATH__), PowerShell and whether it resolves (__PWSH_EXE__, __PWSH_ON_PATH__), this checkout (__PACKAGE_DIR__), the commit it is on (__HEAD__), the composer program with its version and whether it resolves (__COMPOSER_PHAR__, __COMPOSER_VERSION__, __COMPOSER_ON_PATH__), ripgrep with its version and whether it resolves (__RG_EXE__, __RG_VERSION__, __RG_ON_PATH__), the psql client directory (__PSQL_DIR__), the platform's temp directory (__SYSTEM_TEMP_FOLDER__), the signing key git commits with (__GIT_SIGNING_KEY__) and the newest tag the remote answers (__LATEST_TAG__). The rows the repository owns are stated in full rather than tokenised — the origin URL, the checks, the tarball rows and the skill directories — because they are the same in every clone and nothing about them is a fact about the machine being set up. bin/interpreter.php reads php.exe out of the real record and skips the whole file when it is absent, so a clone without one runs on whatever php the shell has; tests/Unit/Docs/HandoffTest.php compares HANDOFF.md's environment table with the real record and skips the comparison here for the same reason."
}
